    "rationale": "Evidence from iteration 0 (420.1 score, 60 trials). Oval finishes 80% of runs, so the baseline handles gentle curvature. S-bend finishes only 10% (18 of 20 off track, progress 0.72), and slalom finishes 0% (progress 0.21, all off track). Line-loss events are 0.95 on oval, 1.2 on s-bend and 1.9 on slalom, while rms_error stays low (0.011 to 0.027 m). Under the Integrator's rule, high line loss with low rms error points at sensor footprint or coverage as the limit, not at lookahead. Steering oscillation is moderate (0.24 to 0.35), so I am not reducing lookahead yet. The current sensors span only about ±0.03 m (±0.024 m centres plus 6 mm half-footprints), so on sharp bends the tape can leave the whole array while the robot is still well inside the 0.09 m off-track limit. Change: widen the array to x = +0.032, +0.016, 0, -0.016, -0.032 and use 16 mm footprints at 16 mm spacing. This gives a contiguous ±0.040 m coverage with no gaps and adjacent footprints just touching. I keep every other field fixed (y 0.06, wheel_track 0.12, mass 0.8, body 0.16 by 0.12, wheel radius 0.03), so the Integrator can attribute any change to sensing. Expected result: line_loss_events fall, and s-bend and slalom progress rise, because the controller keeps a reading as the robot moves off the line. Risk: 16 mm footprints average over a wider area and may blur the signal at small offsets, which could raise rms_error somewhat.",
